1
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:21,000
For political prisoner George Jackson, revolution was
not a choice... it was a necessity

2
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Black August is a drama film directed by Samm Styles.

3
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:51,000
The last 14 months of George Jackson's life was an existence under subjective and
objective conditions in California's industrial prison complex.

4
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
George Jackson would spend 11 years in jail (7 of which were in solitary
confinement) for a $70 gas station robbery crime in 1960.

5
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:21,000
He was 18 years of age when the sentence of one
year-to-life was handed down to him.

6
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:36,000
George Jackson, played by Gary Dourdan.

7
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:51,000
David Dryer, played by Darren Bridgett.

8
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Jonathan Jackson, played by Ezra J. Stanley.

9
01:05:15,000 --> 01:05:21,000
Lumumba, played by 'Big' LeRoy Mobley.

10
01:12:30,000 --> 01:12:36,000
Georgia Jackson, played by Vonetta McGee.

11
01:19:45,000 --> 01:19:51,000
FBI Agent Walker, played by Don Williams.

12
01:27:00,000 --> 01:27:06,000
Black August is a 2007 drama film directed by Samm Styles and starring Gary Dourdan,
Darren Bridgett, Ezra Stanley, "Big" Leroy Mobley, and Don Williams.

13
01:34:15,000 --> 01:34:21,000
It was produced by Tcinque Sampson.

14
01:41:30,000 --> 01:41:36,000
The film centers on the story of George Jackson's life.

15
01:48:45,000 --> 01:48:51,000
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
